---
import Default from "../layouts/Default.astro";
const lastUpdated = "April 26, 2026";
---

<Default
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Alvey Tools: what data we collect, what we don't, and how to reach us."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 prose-tools">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-amber-400 font-semibold mb-3">
      Legal
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-ink-100 mb-3">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="text-ink-400 text-sm mb-10">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This privacy policy applies to the products listed at
      <a href="/" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">alveyautomation.com/tools</a>
      and the Alvey Tools sub-brand of Alvey Automation.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site does</h2>
    <p>
      This is a marketing site. It does not require an account, does not run
      analytics that personally identify you, and does not set advertising
      cookies. Standard server logs (IP address, user agent, request path,
      timestamp) may be retained for operational and security purposes for up
      to 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Per-product data handling</h2>
    <p>
      Each product has its own data-handling story. The summary below
      describes the marketing site only. For per-product specifics, see the
      product page or the product's documentation.
    </p>

    <h3>Marketplace apps (QuickBooks, Shopify, Stripe)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We connect to your account via the marketplace's OAuth flow and
        store only the tokens necessary to perform the documented function.
      </li>
      <li>
        OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest using Fernet (AES-128) with keys
        rotated independently of the database backup schedule.
      </li>
      <li>
        We persist only the aggregates needed for alerts (e.g., per-vendor
        rolling medians, per-SKU velocity numbers, per-recovery state). We
        do not persist customer PII from your accounts.
      </li>
      <li>
        On cancellation we purge your data within 7 days and confirm by
        email when purge completes.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Open-source MCP servers</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        These run locally on your machine. There is no Alvey-hosted backend.
        Your credentials never leave your environment.
      </li>
      <li>
        We do not collect telemetry from the MCP servers. The repos contain
        no analytics or "phone home" hooks.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>One-time downloads (methodology pack, security stack, scaffold)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Purchases are processed by Gumroad, who handles payment data
        according to their own privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        Email addresses provided at purchase are used solely to deliver the
        product and notify you of free updates. We do not sell or share your
        email.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Email contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you email us at <code>brett@alveyautomation.com</code> we will retain
      the conversation for as long as necessary to support you. We do not add
      you to any marketing list without explicit consent.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can request access to, correction of, or deletion of any personal
      data we hold by emailing <code>brett@alveyautomation.com</code>. We
      will respond within 14 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as products evolve. The "Last updated" date
      at the top reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be
      announced via product update emails to existing customers.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <code>brett@alveyautomation.com</code>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Default>
